  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in wooden box (21 x 22 x 5 cm) containing 8 miniature books (5 x 5 cm).</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Savannah College of Art and Design owns all edition numbers 33/80 of the eight miniature books.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Leaves: The leaf photos are from many different places. The cover paper is made from leaves, the font is Vitsui, the printing is Giclee.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Stars: Star photos are by NASA. The cover paper has mica and micro glitter and title is foil stamped. The font is Helvetica, the printing is Giclee.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Rivers: The river photos are from many differnet places in the West. The cover is Japanese screen printed and Ingres blue paper, the font is Bradley Hand. The printing is Giclee.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Rocks: The cover is real rock. The photographs are from many places. The font is Helvetica, the printing is Giclee.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Rainbows: The cover is printable fabric, the font is Lucida Handwriting, the printing is Giclee.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Clouds: Clouds are magnificent examples of nature's details. The cover is cast paper, the font is Khaki, which has been modified, and the printing is Giclee.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Insects: The cover paper is Dhaka, the ants are stamped and thermal embossed. The font is Auriol, the printing is Giclee.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Beach: The beach details were found along the California and Oregon coasts. The cover is polymer clay and Oregon sand, the font is called "Sand" and the printing is Giclee.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="1" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Each minature book has a distinctive title: Beach -- Clouds -- Insects -- Leaves -- Rainbows -- Rivers -- Rocks -- Stars.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1="1" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Jen Library Special Collections copy is numbered 52 out of 40.</subfield>
  </datafield>
